{"name":"Awareness","hex":"#e3ebb1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"awareness","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state or level of consciousness where sense data can be confirmed by an observer.","The state or quality of being aware of something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awareness"}],"entries":[{"title":"Awareness","blocks":[{"text":"Awareness is a state of knowing, understanding, or being conscious of something. Its precise definition is disputed and varies across disciplines. Some accounts treat it as a synonym for consciousness, while others characterize it as cognitive access to information that can occur without subjective experience. Awareness plays a central role in everyday life by helping individuals perceive their surroundings, monitor and regulate their behavior, and make information available to other cognitive processes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Awareness","wikidata":"Q4338318"},{"title":"Awareness (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Awareness is a 2023 Spanish-American science-fiction action thriller film directed by Daniel Benmayor, who also co-wrote the screenplay with Iván Ledesma, and Manuel Burque. It stars Carlos Scholz alongside María Pedraza, Pedro Alonso, Lela Loren, and Óscar Jaenada."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/df/Awareness_2023_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Awareness_(film)","wikidata":"Q121471122"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Young_woman_reading_a_book_closeup.jpg/500px-Young_woman_reading_a_book_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Young_woman_reading_a_book_closeup.jpg/1280px-Young_woman_reading_a_book_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Young_woman_reading_a_book_closeup.jpg/500px-Young_woman_reading_a_book_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Focal awareness encompasses contents at the center of attention, such as a text one is reading, while peripheral awareness encompasses objects outside the focus, such as the surrounding room noticed in the background while reading.[60]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYoung_woman_reading_a_book_closeup.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Mirror_test_with_a_Baboon_%28cropped%29.JPG/500px-Mirror_test_with_a_Baboon_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Mirror_test_with_a_Baboon_%28cropped%29.JPG/500px-Mirror_test_with_a_Baboon_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The mirror test assesses self-awareness in animals by evaluating whether they recognize their reflection in a mirror.[81]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMirror_test_with_a_Baboon_(cropped).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/1206_FMRI.jpg/330px-1206_FMRI.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/1206_FMRI.jpg/330px-1206_FMRI.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Neuroimaging, such as functional magnetic resonance imaging, is one way of studying awareness.[83]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1206_FMRI.jpg"}],"sounds":{"awareness":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/24/En-us-awareness.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wiki